>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must not be floating-point or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 2 (all dimension sizes of the input tensor are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ndim(v_1) - 1 else -1] : i < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (value ranges consistent with common integer dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then min(v_1) ≥ -128 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 127 else if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 255
>>
Rule 4 (sequence of tensors input must be non-empty)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (sequence of tensors has a reasonable maximum size)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len ≤ 65536
>>
Rule 6 (valid iteration bounds over the sequence indices)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= if v_1.len = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : 0 ≤ i ∧ i ≤ v_1.len - 1
>>
Rule 7 (input tensor should not already be fp32)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 7
>>
Rule 8 (list-of-tensors parameter is well-formed)
{v_1 : list(tensor)} |= v_1 = v_1
